my":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Prodigal Sorcerer","oracle_id":"5e961d15-5972-4e4b-9385-1cd7cd7c6bbe","oracle_text":"{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-06-10","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Human Wizard Sorcerer"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Split second"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{R}{R}","name":"Word of Seizing","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","oracle_text":"Split second (As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.)\nUntap target permanent and gain control of it until end of turn. It gains haste until end of turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"After a spell with split second resolves (or otherwise leaves the stack), players may again cast spells and activate abilities before the next object on the stack resolves.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting a spell with split second won't affect spells and abilities that are already on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the resolution of a triggered ability involves casting a spell, that spell can't be cast if a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players still get priority while a card with split second is on the stack; their options are just limited to mana abilities and certain special actions.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities from triggering, such as that of Chalice of the Void. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of Contested War Zone doesn’t cause it to tap or untap.","oracle_id":"ed73de2b-d7f4-48d9-9be2-aa9d111b7aa7","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In some multiplayer formats, creatures controlled by different players may deal combat damage to you simultaneously. If this happens, you control each triggered ability and can put them on the stack in any order. The last ability to resolve will determine who ends up controlling Contested War Zone.","oracle_id":"ed73de2b-d7f4-48d9-9be2-aa9d111b7aa7","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last activated ability affects all attacking creatures, not just those you control.","oracle_id":"ed73de2b-d7f4-48d9-9be2-aa9d111b7aa7","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The word “you” in a permanent’s trigger condition always refers to the permanent’s current controller.","oracle_id":"ed73de2b-d7f4-48d9-9be2-aa9d111b7aa7","published_at":"2011-06-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
